> 
> ### Steps to Fix the Errors
> 
> 1. **Remove or Comment Out Broken Repositories**:
> 
>    First, you need to open the sources list and PPA files to identify and remove/comment out the problematic entries.
> 
>    **Open the main sources list file**:
> 
>    ```bash
>    sudo nano /etc/apt/sources.list
>    ```
> 
>    **Check additional PPA files**:
> 
>    ```bash
>    ls /etc/apt/sources.list.d/
>    ```
> 
>    You'll find files named like `repository-name.list`. Open those that include the problematic RabbitMQ and Mendeley repositories.
> 
>    For instance:
> 
>    ```bash
>    sudo nano /etc/apt/sources.list.d/rabbitmq.list
>    ```
> 
>    Look for lines like:
>    ```plaintext
>    deb https://ppa1.novemberain.com/rabbitmq/rabbitmq-erlang/deb/ubuntu jammy main
>    deb https://desktop-download.mendeley.com/download/apt stable main
>    ```
> 
>    Comment them out by adding a `#` at the beginning of each line or remove them entirely. Save and exit (Ctrl + O, Enter, Ctrl + X).
> 
> 2. **Update Package Lists Again**:
> 
>    After you've made changes, try updating the package lists again:
> 
>    ```bash
>    sudo apt-get update
>    ```
